  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday Night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1120 AM CDT Sat Aug 8 2026\n\nHeading into Monday and Tuesday, upper level ridging will become \na little stronger as the big, hot ridge from out west bridges \nacross to the persistent Bermuda high. This will bump temperatures\nup a little while slightly reducing shower and storm coverage (10\npercent northwest to 40 percent southeast). Heat index values \nlook marginal for heat headlines, but caution is advised with Heat\nRisk levels reaching level 3 out of 4 (Major) for most areas. \nHeat headlines may be issued for some areas west of the Plateau \nover the next couple of days if forecast data trend hotter.\n\nGoing through the week, it will stay hot and humid with daily\nchances for showers and storms. There are some important model\ndifferences that could impact the forecast late week. Looking at \nLREF clustering data, we see big differences emerging between the \nGFS and ECMWF groups. The GFS is trending toward a broad eastern \ntrough with the potential for increased storminess and less heat while\nthe ECMWF camp is building up the ridge across the southern \nstates and TN Valley. This would mean lower storm chances and \nhotter conditions with temps well into the 90s. Time will tell, \nbut neither scenario would be terribly out of line for August.",
